&lt;div class="panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="article-hero"&gt;
&lt;div class="article-type"&gt;Case Study · Google Ads · AI Agent&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1 class="article-title"&gt;Google Ads MCP: How an AI Agent Runs Your Ads Without Burning the Budget&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="article-lead"&gt;An AI agent can run Google Ads, but Google's official Google Ads MCP server is read-only, so safe changes need your own backend with business rules. On a real account, the average CPC went from 0.82 EUR (July) to 0.47 EUR (August to September 2026) at about 9 EUR a day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="article-lead"&gt;I am Mikhail Azhyshchev, an AI-Enabled Automation Engineer in Munich. This page shows what I built, what the numbers on a real small-budget account look like, and why the agent never talks to the Google Ads API directly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="metrics-row"&gt;
&lt;div class="metric-box"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;0.82 → 0.47 EUR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Average CPC, windows and campaign counts in the results table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="metric-box"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;~8.92 EUR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Spend per day across 4 countries (DE, AT, ES, FR)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="metric-box"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;909&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Real search queries reviewed in one 30 day audit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="metric-box"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;22.07 EUR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Leak found and stopped: 11 clicks, 0 sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="article-body"&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;The need&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;What businesses actually want from Google Ads automation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nobody I talk to asks for an "AI agent". They describe a problem, and it is almost always one of these four:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paying more per click than the market asks.&lt;/strong&gt; A bid ceiling set once and never revisited quietly drifts above what the clicks are worth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget leaking into searches that were never meant for you.&lt;/strong&gt; The ad shows for a product you do not sell, and every click is paid at full price.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nobody has time to read the search terms report.&lt;/strong&gt; It is the most useful page in the account and the one that gets opened least.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Small budgets rarely fit an agency retainer.&lt;/strong&gt; A Google Ads budget of a few euros a day rarely justifies a full-service retainer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An AI agent is a reasonable answer to all four, because the recurring work is reading, comparing and making small adjustments. That is exactly what software does well. The open question is not whether an agent can do it. The open question is what stands between the agent and your money.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;The risk&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Why you should not plug an AI agent straight into Google Ads&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Start with what Google itself says. Google's official Google Ads MCP server is read-only in the current release. Its documentation calls it "strictly read-only" and states that it cannot modify bids, pause campaigns or create new assets. It offers three tools: list the accessible accounts, run a query in Google's query language (GAQL) and read resource metadata. That is useful for reports and audits, and nothing more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So the moment you want the agent to change something, it needs write access to the Google Ads API itself. Two facts from Google's developer documentation matter here:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The API has no object locking. If two edits hit the same object at the same time, the API answers with a CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION_ERROR instead of protecting you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google recommends that you use test accounts, prefer read-only requests where possible, set validate_only on change requests, and review the change history afterwards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read between the lines: the API executes what it is sent. It does not know that a bid is absurd for the product you sell. It does not know your business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What can go wrong in plain words&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent raises a bid ceiling by a large jump because a report looked good for two days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent enables a campaign that you paused on purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent edits the wrong field and overwrites a setting you never meant to touch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None of these are exotic. They are what happens when a capable tool has permission and no rules. A generic Google Ads MCP server with write access gives the agent the permission. It cannot give it your rules, because it has never seen your business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;The setup&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;What a safe Google Ads MCP setup looks like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The agent never touches the Google Ads API. It talks to my backend: a custom MCP server with business logic in front of the API. The backend decides what is allowed, and the API only ever sees requests that passed. In practice this means five rules, written in plain words:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="check-list"&gt;
&lt;div class="check-item"&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;1. A health check before any work&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Before the agent may use a single ad tool, it must pass a check of the tooling, of changes made outside the agent, and of the process state. If something looks off, the owner has to confirm before work continues.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="check-item"&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;2. Hard bid limits and small steps&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;span&gt;A bid ceiling has a floor and a ceiling that live in code, and it can only move in small steps. A big jump is not something the agent can talk its way into.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="check-item"&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;3. Negative keyword lists per country, plus duplicate detection&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Each country has its own list of searches you never want to pay for. The backend also finds keywords that compete against each other across your own campaigns.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="check-item"&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;4. Change only the named field&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Every change says exactly which setting it touches. Everything else in the campaign stays as it was.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="check-item"&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;5. A journal of every action&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Every call is written down with the time, the tool, whether it only read or really changed something, the result and a trace ID. You can answer "what happened and why" weeks later without asking anyone.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight-box"&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;FastMCP Evolution: What's New in v1.1.0 (November 2026)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The system has evolved from an internal prototype into an enterprise open-source framework, now expanded to &lt;strong&gt;59 purpose-built tools&lt;/strong&gt; and battle-tested across 237 offline unit tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;59 Tools (+23 Added):&lt;/strong&gt; Deep lifecycle management for ad groups, image assets, geo-targeting, conversion goals, and search term mining.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Google Shopping &amp;amp; Merchant Center Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Audits feed readiness (&lt;code&gt;check_shopping_readiness&lt;/code&gt;) across Merchant Center IDs and products before campaigns can be touched. Every new shopping campaign is forced to &lt;strong&gt;PAUSED&lt;/strong&gt; by design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Policy as Data:&lt;/strong&gt; All company rules (account IDs, forbidden negative terms, allowed hosts, coupon parameters) are isolated in a git-ignored &lt;code&gt;config/policy.local.json&lt;/code&gt; file. Code is 100% agnostic and zero-leak.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hard Invariants:&lt;/strong&gt; The agent is physically blocked from deleting your last target country, cannot enable an empty ad group, and steps CPC ceilings strictly by ±0.05 EUR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;W3C Distributed Tracing:&lt;/strong&gt; Full observability capturing Google upstream request IDs and separating local validation latency from Google gRPC execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;237 Offline Tests:&lt;/strong&gt; 100% validation suite runs in 2.2 seconds without spending a cent on live APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div style="margin-top:16px;padding:12px 16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.06);border-radius:8px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Open-Source Framework on GitHub:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style="margin:2px 0 0 0;font-size:14px;color:#cbd5e1;"&gt;Clone the engine, set your business rules in JSON, and connect Claude Code or Cursor safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;a class="cta-btn" href="https://github.com/Azhy34/safe-google-ads-mcp" rel="noreferrer" style="font-size:13px;padding:8px 16px;" target="_blank"&gt;View on GitHub →&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top:12px;"&gt;&lt;a href="/projects/ai-ads-management/?utm_source=portfolio&amp;amp;utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_campaign=google-ads-mcp-ai-agent&amp;amp;utm_content=engineering_case_link"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Deep-Dive: FastMCP Architecture, Tracing &amp;amp; Post-Run Evals →&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;Cost per click&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Google Ads cost: buying clicks at the low end of the market&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The account is a real one: a boutique e-commerce brand selling home &amp;amp; children's decor, with campaigns in Germany, Austria, Spain and France. The bid strategy is Maximize clicks with a CPC ceiling per campaign. In plain terms: Google may buy as many clicks as the budget allows, but never above the price I set for each campaign.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here is how the average Google CPC moved:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0.82 EUR before the cleanup (120.03 EUR for 147 clicks, 05.07-04.08.2026, 2 campaigns).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0.53 EUR for the same 2 campaigns once the cleanup had started (21.07-04.08.2026).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0.47 EUR across all 6 spending campaigns (276.66 EUR for 592 clicks, 18.08-17.09.2026). Per campaign the range was 0.45 to 0.55 EUR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Google Ads budget behind this is small: 276.66 EUR in 31 days, about 8.92 EUR per day across 4 countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;A conscious trade-off, not a bidding war&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In September the impression share was 10 to 20 percent, and the share lost to ad rank was 63 to 80 percent (18.08-17.09). That looks bad until you know the plan. The plan said: do not chase the maximum bid, take 10 percent impression share with a CPC in range instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The audit also showed why. Raising the ceiling without improving the landing pages would only burn money. We do not pay for top positions, and a low ad rank is a useful signal: it tells us where the landing pages need work before more money goes in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;Traffic quality&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Google Ads plus GA4: see what the traffic does&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clicks are only half of the picture. I join Google Ads with GA4, so the agent sees not just what a click cost, but what the visitor did afterwards. For 05.07-04.08.2026 the join shows 235 sessions from google/cpc, 72 percent of them engaged, with an average of 1m30s on the site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same join catches leaks that a cost report alone never shows. The agent reviewed 909 real search queries from 30 days (mid-July to 15.08.2026), and a negative keyword shield of 21 terms went live for the DE and AT campaigns. What the review found:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A wrong-product leak.&lt;/strong&gt; Searches for "Wandtattoo" and "Wandsticker" are a different product than wallpaper. On 04.08.2026 they had cost 22.07 EUR for 11 clicks and 0 sales, which is 18.4 percent of the 30 day spend. That ad group was paused the same day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;36 duplicate keywords&lt;/strong&gt; that competed with each other were paused (04.08.2026). Your own keywords should not compete against each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 broad keywords&lt;/strong&gt; that had cost 44.85 EUR in 30 days were paused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No single item here is dramatic. Together they are the difference between an account that drifts and one that is looked after every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;Deterministic Pipeline &amp;amp; Audit Log&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Data Flow &amp;amp; Real-Time Execution Journal&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An AI agent should never talk directly to ad APIs. Every action passes through a four-stage deterministic gate in FastMCP. Below is how data moves through the shield, followed by an excerpt from the production execution journal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;!-- Pipeline Flow Diagram --&gt;
&lt;div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));gap:12px;margin:16px 0 20px 0;"&gt;
&lt;div style="background:var(--cream);border:2px solid var(--black);padding:12px;box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--black);"&gt;
&lt;div style="font-size:0.7rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#555;"&gt;Stage 1: Intent&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong style="display:block;margin:4px 0;font-size:0.85rem;"&gt;Agent Prompt Parsing&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:0.76rem;line-height:1.45;color:#333;"&gt;Claude Code proposes an operation via tool call with explicit arguments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="background:var(--yellow);border:2px solid var(--black);padding:12px;box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--black);"&gt;
&lt;div style="font-size:0.7rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#555;"&gt;Stage 2: Policy&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong style="display:block;margin:4px 0;font-size:0.85rem;"&gt;Policy-as-Data Check&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:0.76rem;line-height:1.45;color:#333;"&gt;Matches against &lt;code&gt;policy.local.json&lt;/code&gt;: CID bounds, negative whitelist, host domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="background:var(--peach);border:2px solid var(--black);padding:12px;box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--black);"&gt;
&lt;div style="font-size:0.7rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#555;"&gt;Stage 3: Invariants&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong style="display:block;margin:4px 0;font-size:0.85rem;"&gt;Preflight Hard Guards&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:0.76rem;line-height:1.45;color:#333;"&gt;Blocks empty ad groups, enforces ±0.05€ bid steps, asserts active geo count ≥ 1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="background:var(--mint);border:2px solid var(--black);padding:12px;box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--black);"&gt;
&lt;div style="font-size:0.7rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#555;"&gt;Stage 4: Execution&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;strong style="display:block;margin:4px 0;font-size:0.85rem;"&gt;Surgical Mutation &amp;amp; Trace&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:0.76rem;line-height:1.45;color:#333;"&gt;Sends Google gRPC update mask; commits W3C trace ID and upstream Request ID.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;!-- Execution Journal Table --&gt;
&lt;div class="table-wrap"&gt;
&lt;table class="data-table" style="font-size:0.76rem;"&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th style="width:70px;"&gt;Time&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Tool Called&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="width:75px;"&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Target / Payload&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Guardrail &amp;amp; Policy Verdict&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="width:115px;"&gt;Status / Latency&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:02:11&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;check_preflight_gate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--sky);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;HEALTH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CID: &lt;code&gt;753-***-****&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;All preflight checks green. Operating policy v1.1.0 active.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#166534;"&gt;PASSED&lt;/span&gt; (38ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:02:15&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;audit_search_terms&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--cream);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;READ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Campaign: &lt;code&gt;Search_Core&lt;/code&gt; (7d spend &amp;gt; 0)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;184 queries parsed. 4 non-intent search patterns flagged.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#166534;"&gt;200 OK&lt;/span&gt; (215ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:02:28&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;add_campaign_negatives&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--yellow);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;MUTATE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Negatives: &lt;code&gt;[free, crack, diy, test]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Exact match. Checked against negative whitelist. Zero leak.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#166534;"&gt;APPLIED&lt;/span&gt; (310ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:03:04&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;update_cpc_ceiling&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--yellow);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;MUTATE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;0.55€ → 0.50€&lt;/code&gt; (Search_Core)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Step invariant verified: Δ = -0.05€ (within ±0.05€ boundary).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#166534;"&gt;MUTATED&lt;/span&gt; (240ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="background:#fed7aa;"&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:03:22&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;set_adgroup_status&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--coral);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;MUTATE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;AdGroup &lt;code&gt;#49102&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;ENABLE&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Invariant Triggered:&lt;/strong&gt; Target group has 0 active ads. Spend blocked.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:800;color:#991b1b;background:#fee2e2;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #991b1b;"&gt;BLOCKED&lt;/span&gt; (14ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:03:45&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;check_shopping_readiness&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--sky);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;AUDIT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Merchant Center: &lt;code&gt;284910***&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Feed synced. 1 product pending review → shopping campaign held PAUSED.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#1e3a8a;"&gt;HELD&lt;/span&gt; (190ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14:04:10&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;write_audit_telemetry&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="display:inline-block;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid #111;background:var(--cream);font-size:0.68rem;font-weight:800;"&gt;SYSTEM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;W3C Trace ID: &lt;code&gt;4bf92f35...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Upstream Google Request ID committed to persistent audit log.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:700;color:#166534;"&gt;SYNCED&lt;/span&gt; (22ms)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="prose" style="margin-top:14px;"&gt;
&lt;p class="source-note"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this matters to the business owner (Notice Row 5):&lt;/strong&gt; When the agent attempted to activate an unready ad group, the deterministic Python shield blocked the mutation locally in &lt;strong&gt;14ms&lt;/strong&gt; before sending a single gRPC byte to Google Ads. Your budget is physically guarded by hard code invariants, not prompt promises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
