&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;The honest part&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Why this is engineering work, not a plugin, and who it suits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="prose"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You cannot install safe Google Ads management as a plugin. The value sits in the rules: how high a bid may go, how fast it may move, which searches you never want, and who has to confirm when something looks off. Those rules are different in every business, so somebody has to write them down and build them into the tooling. That is the engineering work I do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It suits you if:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You spend roughly 5-50 EUR a day in the DACH region and want control over where it goes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want routine Google Ads management done every day, not whenever somebody has a free hour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to see what was changed and why, in a journal you can read yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It does not suit you if you want a full-service agency that also handles strategy, creative and client meetings. For that, hire an agency. If the business-side question is where your money leaks across all channels, start with the article &lt;a href="/articles/ai-google-ads-management/?utm_source=portfolio&amp;amp;utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_campaign=google-ads-mcp-ai-agent&amp;amp;utm_content=related_article"&gt;One control panel for every ad channel you run&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="cta-strip"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Want to know what your own account is leaking?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 30 minutes we look at your search terms and your bid ceilings and decide whether an agent backend makes sense for you. If it does not, you still leave with a list of what to block.&lt;/p&gt;
