&lt;div class="neo-card"&gt;
&lt;div class="section-label"&gt;FAQ&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Questions people ask before letting an AI agent touch their ads&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="faq"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;Can an AI agent manage my Google Ads account on its own?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;Yes for the routine work: reading reports, finding wasted spend, adding negative keywords and moving a bid ceiling in small steps. No for unsupervised access to the raw API, because the API executes whatever it is sent. The agent should talk to a backend that holds your rules, checks its own state before it starts and writes a journal of every action.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;Is the official Google Ads MCP server enough?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;For reading, yes. Google's docs describe the official server as strictly read-only: it lists accounts, runs GAQL queries and returns resource metadata, but it cannot modify bids, pause campaigns or create assets. To change anything, an agent needs mutate access to the Google Ads API, and that is where your own backend with business rules comes in.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;What does Google Ads cost with a small budget?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;It depends on your market, so I only quote my own account. A boutique e-commerce shop spent 276.66 EUR in 31 days, about 8.92 EUR per day across Germany, Austria, Spain and France, at an average CPC of 0.47 EUR. Small budgets work when waste is removed early and bid ceilings stay low.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;Can Claude manage Google Ads?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;A model like Claude can read reports, spot patterns in search terms and propose changes. What it may actually change depends on the tools behind it. Connected straight to the API it can break things, so I put a backend between the agent and Google Ads: hard bid limits, a health check before work and a journal of every call.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;How do I stop an AI agent from overspending?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;Do not rely on the model being careful. Put the limits in code. In my setup a bid ceiling cannot leave the range of 0.10 to 3.00 EUR and moves only in steps of 0.05 EUR. On 05.10.2026 a malformed ceiling change was rejected and nothing was changed. Every call is written to a journal you can read.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-item"&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-q"&gt;Do I still need a Google Ads agency?&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="faq-a"&gt;It depends on what you need. If you want a full-service agency for strategy, creative and reporting, an agent setup is not a replacement. If you run a small or mid-size account and want control over routine checks, search terms and bid ceilings, a custom agent backend covers that work, and you can see every action in the journal.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="cta-strip"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Let an agent do the routine, keep the decisions&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tell me your daily budget and your countries. We check whether a safe agent setup is worth it for your account.&lt;/p&gt;
